## Why This Is Asked
This tests practical gating of Terraform plans using a dedicated QA backend, plan export, and automated validation to prevent prod touches.

## Key Concepts
- Backend aliasing and per-env state isolation
- terraform plan output in JSON
- Scripting plan validation with jq/Node.js
- CI gating and manual approvals for apply

## Code Example
```javascript
// Node.js snippet to validate plan.json plan boundaries
const fs=require('fs');
const plan=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('plan.json','utf8'));
const resources=plan?.planned_values?.root_module?.resources||[];
const ok=resources.every(r=>r.address.startsWith('modules/qa/')||r.address.includes('environment=qa'));
process.exit(ok?0:1);
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you extend this to multi-module repos?
- How do you handle drift checks beyond plan validation?
